Package: oneqnode
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: oneq <k@1q.ro>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: python3 (>= 3.13), python3 (<< 3.14), libssl3t64 (>= 3.5), iproute2, adduser, util-linux
Suggests: oneqrelay, supervisor
Section: net
Priority: optional
Description: node of the oneq post-quantum layer-2 mesh (virtual Ethernet)
 oneqnode joins a community hosted by one or more oneqrelay servers. It logs
 in with a user name and password, receives an IP and a MAC address
 automatically, and opens end-to-end sessions with every other member:
 directly over UDP (with hole punching) or through the relay when that
 fails. Ethernet frames are switched between a TAP interface and the
 sessions, so the community behaves like one LAN.
 .
 Sessions use a hybrid X25519 + ML-KEM-768 handshake and
 ChaCha20-Poly1305. Several oneqrelay servers can be configured for
 failover; established sessions keep working when all of them are down.
 .
 Installed in /opt/oneq/node, configured by /etc/oneq/node.conf. Runs under systemd or supervisord. Needs Python 3.13 linked against OpenSSL 3.5 or newer (Debian 13). The
 Python libraries it uses are bundled in /opt/oneq/node/site-packages.
 This is an educational project without an independent security audit.
